# AI agent manager

One command for local AI coding-agent hygiene and the indexed Agent Skills
ecosystem. The registry covers Codex, Claude Code, Gemini CLI, Copilot CLI,
Qwen Code, OpenCode, Kilo, Cline, Aider, goose, Vibe, Amp, Cursor, Kiro,
Droid, OpenHands, Pi, and Rovo Dev. Market discovery delegates to the live
`skills` CLI index without claiming that any index contains every public or
private skill.

> **Trust boundary:** Every `market` search or install runs
> `npx --yes skills@1.5.22 ...`. It requires Node.js, `npx`, and network access and
> may download and execute the pinned npm package. Review that package and
> each skill source before continuing.

## Actions

### `doctor`

Finds installed executables, runs version checks, validates JSON/TOML settings,
checks state-directory permissions, locates the agent's skill directory, and
distinguishes a missing executable with leftover state from an installed client
that has not initialized its state root.
YAML, YAML-derived, and JSONC files are reported as **not parsed**, not as
validated. Select `--fix` to preview owner-only permission repairs. Missing
skill directories are normal and remain the responsibility of the selected
market installer; applying does not install agents or rewrite their settings.

### `clean`

Use `--kind sessions`, `--kind memories`, `--kind cache`, or `--kind all`.
Only documented local state is targeted. Credentials, API keys, configuration,
skills, plugins, `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `GEMINI.md`, and equivalent
project-authored instructions are excluded.

Every preview reports the number of local entries and their logical byte size
without following symlinks. Native vendor operations are counted separately
because their reclaimable size is unavailable before deletion.

Codex, OpenCode, and Kilo conversations are enumerated and deleted with native
non-interactive commands. Codex's documented global `history.jsonl` is also
removed for session cleanup. OpenHands conversation directories and Pi JSONL
sessions use their documented local deletion contracts. Gemini's native
listing is shown, then deletion is handed off to
`gemini --delete-session INDEX_OR_ID` because its human-readable listing is not
a stable machine interface. Claude's native purge combines conversations,
auto-memory, and related project state, so it is available only through
`clean all`; that explicit operation previews every project recorded by Claude
before applying. Aider's documented history files remain current-project
scoped.

Managed Copilot, goose, and Cline session databases are never deleted. Use
Copilot's `/session delete`, `/session delete-all`, or `/session prune` UI,
`goose session` commands, or `cline history` instead. Qwen's native session
listing and interactive memory commands remain manual because it has no
documented noninteractive delete-all contract. Other clients without a
verified, separable conversation store have no automatic session target.

Close affected agents before applying.

### Authority boundary

Direct path removal is local only. Native vendor commands run without remote
flags and keep their documented local CLI scope. The command does not access or
delete provider-account, cloud, synchronized, Hub, IDE, or retention records;
Copilot, Amp, Kilo Cloud, Cline Hub, OpenHands Cloud, and Factory Cloud Sync may
retain separate copies. Gemini session listing is current-project scoped.
`market` is the only workflow that intentionally uses the network.

### `market`

Enter a `--query` to search interactively. To preview an install, set
`--install owner/repository`, optionally `--skill name`, and select `--global`
for user scope. The default `all` target uses the installer's supported `*`
agent target; choose one `--agent` to narrow it. A preview lists what the live
package would install; it does not establish that the source is trustworthy.

## Direct CLI

```sh
agent doctor --list-agents
agent doctor --agent codex --fix
agent clean sessions --agent gemini-cli
agent clean all --agent claude-code
agent clean all --agent codex --apply
agent clean sessions --agent kilo
agent clean sessions --agent pi
agent market "Python security"
agent market --install vercel-labs/agent-skills --skill find-skills --agent codex
```

Without `--apply`, destructive and repair commands only print their plan.
Direct applies require typing `APPLY`; the shared TUI performs its own `CLEAN`
confirmation and then supplies `--apply --yes`. Vendor commands invoked by the
TUI are read-only, explicitly forced, or passed a vendor confirmation flag and
never expect input from the TUI's closed standard input.

See `docs/agent-tools.md` for researched storage, diagnostics, market
compatibility, and limitations.

## Exit status

`0` means the selected local operation completed. `1` means a doctor check or
cleanup target failed or was blocked. `2` means the command could not run
safely. `market` otherwise returns the live `skills` command's status.
